Falsifies `file_allocation_table::directory_writer::verification::the_first_free_alias_number_is_the_least_one_not_marked`.

The defect: the first free number is counted by the word's trailing zeros instead of its trailing
ones, so a window whose first number is free reports a later number, and with every low number
taken it reports one already taken, which the writer would give to a second entry.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(marks.contains(&below))`.

diff --git a/src/directory_writer.rs b/src/directory_writer.rs
--- a/src/directory_writer.rs
+++ b/src/directory_writer.rs
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ impl<const WORDS: usize> AliasWindow<WORDS> {
             .iter()
             .enumerate()
             .find(|(_, word)| **word != u64::MAX)?;
-        Some(self.first + at as u32 * 64 + word.trailing_ones())
+        Some(self.first + at as u32 * 64 + word.trailing_zeros())
     }
 }
 
